  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member using Increase Contrast in dark mode, I want the \"non lu\" capsule of the MP list to stay readable, so that the setting does not make it harder to read than the default.\n\nRefs #576 (found in its Mac check).\n\n### Observed\nBuild 4b1e77f5, iPhone 18 Pro and iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) simulators, iOS 27.0. `MessageRowView`: white `caption2` on `Color(.systemGray)`.\n\n| Setting | Capsule fill, measured | White text contrast |\n|---|---|---|\n| Light or dark | 142,142,147 | 3.3:1 |\n| Increase Contrast, light | 108,108,112 | 5.3:1 |\n| Increase Contrast, dark | 174,174,178 | **2.2:1** |\n\n`systemGray` gets lighter under Increase Contrast in dark while the text stays white, so the setting lowers the contrast. Seen on fixture rows and on a real list.\n\nAt half strength (the member has read the thread, legacy `MPListView.swift:435` @ 2440d79) the capsule is pale in every mode: about 1.7:1 in light. That half strength is legacy parity; say whether it stays.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- With Increase Contrast in dark, the full-strength capsule is at least as readable as in default dark.\n- Decision recorded on the half-strength capsule (keep legacy, or raise it).\n",
